"FIRST PROD SESSION POSTMORTEM (2026-08-13): login over wss THROUGH THE PROXY WORKED end to end. Then lockout on reload -- root cause OURS, not infra: client_connected REJECTED any attached identity whose account has no player entity, and the bootstrap admin account is exactly that (bootstrap_admin creates the account alone, necessarily before assets exist). The operator's reconnect was therefore refused by our own reducer. FIX (5687b6a): playerless accounts are legitimate at connect; heal late -- create the player on connect once the new-player blob exists, else connect playerless with admin ops available. Recovery story for the live instance after redeploy: reconnect succeeds playerless -> (password already rotated by operator) auto-push runs on admin attach -> next reload creates the admin's player -> play. ATOMICITY (operator concern): push_assets is ONE reducer call = ONE SpacetimeDB transaction; any Err rolls back everything, so a failed push leaves NO partial assets by construction -- the empty world they saw means the pre-rotation push simply failed wholesale at require_admin. Auth-flow e2e (0/1/6/7/12/13) green on the fix."